Patterns can match exact values, ranges, choice variants or option shapes.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if status is {
        case Ready: io.line("ready")
        case Waiting: io.line("waiting")
    }
]

A choice match can omit `else:` when it covers every variant with unguarded arms. A guarded choice match needs a fallback.

Payload variants expose their fields through captures:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if response is {
        case Success: io.line("done")
        case Err(message): io.line(message)
    }
]

The capture name must match the field name.

Use `as` when the local name should be different:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    case Err(message as error_text): io.line(error_text)
]

Options have two complete shapes: absent and present.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if maybe_name is {
        case none: io.line("missing")
        case |name|: io.line(name)
    }
]

Most other value matches need `else:` because the compiler cannot list every
possible `I32`, `String` or other scalar value.
